Hey, I thought nethack had taken the direction that the behavior of holy
water, or blessed items of any kind, does not depend on your alignment.
E.g., assuming you are chaotic, putting potions of water on a chaotic
altar and praying gives you holy water, not unholy water.
Dipping a scroll into holy water blesses (or uncurses) the scroll,
regardless of your alignment.
And reading a blessed scroll of enchant weapon does the same thing
regardless of your alignment.

This thing about chaotics suffering from drinking holy water sounds
like an inconsistency.

Undead should suffer from holy water, and perhaps demons, but not chaotic
players.

Blessing/cursing should not have anything to do with alignment.
If it did, then a lot of other things would have to be changed to
be consistent with this.  E.g. reading a cursed scroll should do 
for chaotics what a blessed scroll does for lawful players.
And that would be problematic because then a helm of opposite alignment
could make all your cursed items behave as though blessed.
And for neutral players, would uncursed items be extra beneficial, cursed
items be worse, and blessed items be normal?

I think the clearest path is to separate blessing/cursing from alignment
as much as possible.

